The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports say otherwise.
They were merged because their subjects matched ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and a matching subject only tells you the date was wrong, not why.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row below. The other two need their own fixes,
so the reports behind them will keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="mrpia/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }} />

**parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on this ticket writes
the day first. 7 April becomes 4 July. This is the bug the ticket was named after, and most of the queue.

**hint.** Tenants on `booking-v3` print `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their customers do as told,
and the form then reads the value day first. Same symptom, different code: only form reports from
alder.physio, copper.studio and pale.harbour. The same tenants' app and email reports are the parser bug.

**one-day.** A handful of reports are not a swap at all. Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May, a
meeting lands on different days in Lisbon and Toronto, an invite arrives before the booking was made.
The desk already listed them as a one-day move in `desk-notes.json`. A date-only value is going
through a time zone somewhere. The table counts them here, under their own ticket.

## How the desk's own view files them

`CauseTable` files by tenant, so the one-day moves sit under `parser` and only get a footnote.
The row it marks as "no ticket of its own" now has one.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For triage

- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It was wrong for a good share of this ticket.
  Use the tenant's locale and form (`causeOf` in `causes.ts`), and the channel.
- A report that names two dates which are not a day/month swap is not this ticket's main bug. Read the body.
- The export pages overlap. Count unique report ids, never rows.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
